content.text:
Done. All tests pass and no new lints — the 5 remaining are pre-existing (the untouched `factory`-ordering and multi-var lines in `energy_history.dart`) or match the existing test file's `Int64(0x…)` hex style.

## What changed

In `lib/models/energy_history.dart`, `EnergyHistoryData.fromProto` now drops the in-progress bucket before building anything:

```dart
// The bucket containing the query's end time is still in progress: it holds
// only the energy accrued so far this interval, so it always reads low and
// climbs as the interval fills. Drop it (and anything at/after it) ...
final to = h.to.toInt();
final inProgressIndex = to > start ? (to - start) ~/ bucketSec : 1 << 30;
final buckets = [
  for (final b in h.buckets)
    if (b.index < inProgressIndex) b,
];
```

Key points:
- **Identified via the controller's own `to`/`start`/`bucketSeconds`**, so it uses the controller's clock — no phone-wall-clock skew, and the whole change is app-side (no firmware needed).
- **Chart *and* totals stay consistent** — everything downstream (points, KPI totals, per-PV device series) is derived from the filtered list, so `sum(pvSeries.kwh) == pvKwh` still holds. The chart now ends on the last *complete* hour instead of a diving partial one.
- **Boundary-safe**: when `to` lands exactly on a bucket boundary, the empty/future bucket is excluded and the complete hours are kept.
- **Backward-compatible**: the `to > start` guard means older/`to`-unset responses (and all existing tests) get no cutoff.

Two tests added: one asserting the partial trailing bucket is excluded from chart and totals, one for the exact-boundary case.

Trade-off to be aware of: the "consumed · 12 h" headline and KPIs now exclude the current partial hour, so they read as "complete hours only" — slightly more conservative, but consistent with the chart and no longer misleading.

This is unit-tested but not yet running on a device (the installed app is the older release). Want me to `flutter build apk --release` and reinstall on the Pixel (and the Nothing Phone) so you can see it live?
